# pkg/gateway C3 regroup manifest (proposal 0020, Part B C1).
#
# Machine-readable move manifest the C3 driver (scripts/refactor) consumes to
# regroup pkg/gateway's flat sibling subpackages into intermediate, spec-aligned
# group directories. Authored by Part B C1; executed by Part B C3.
#
# Format: one move per line, two tab-separated fields:
#     <old fully-qualified import path>\t<new fully-qualified import path>
# Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are comments. The driver (proposal
# §2) per entry: git mv the directory; rewrite the quote-delimited import
# literal "<old>" -> "<new>" across *.go (boundary-anchored on the closing
# quote, so a moved path that is a strict prefix of a sibling import does not
# corrupt the sibling); rewrite the matching slash-joined and split path-segment
# runtime-read references; rewrite the same tokens in tests/spec-map.json and
# tests/change-graph.json on a path-token boundary; gofmt/goimports; gate on
# go build, go vet, and lenny-test validate-maps; regenerate the CodeGraph index.
# Package names are unchanged, so no identifier rewrites are needed.
#
# Group taxonomy and the spec section each group maps to: pkg/gateway/ARCHITECTURE.md.
#
# Excluded from this manifest (handled elsewhere; see ARCHITECTURE.md):
#   pkg/gateway/events        -> split by Part B C2 into pkg/events (shared
#                                vocabulary, out of the gateway) and
#                                pkg/gateway/eventbuffer (the §25.3 buffer).
#   pkg/gateway/sessionserver -> stays whole at the gateway root; it realizes
#                                the §4.1 Stream Proxy and Upload Handler behind
#                                their interfaces and is not split across groups.
#   pkg/gateway/middleware    -> already an intermediate group directory; it
#                                stays at the gateway root. breakerstore nests
#                                under its existing middleware/circuitbreaker
#                                package (the §1.3 gateway-core re-anchor).
#
# §1.3 exclusions encoded below:
#   breakerstore     -> middleware/circuitbreaker/breakerstore (anchors into
#                       gateway-core, not the persistence cluster).
#   interceptorstore -> policy/interceptor/interceptorstore (anchors onto its
#                       interceptor core dependency).
#   policy           -> policy/policy (§4.8 engine stays embedded in the gateway).
#   environmentstore -> environment/environmentstore (§10.6, gateway-internal).
#   experiment*      -> experiment/* (§10.7, gateway-internal).
#
# §2 subsystem-seam decision encoded below: §4.1 assigns delegation to the MCP
# Fabric subsystem, so the delegation-tree lifecycle packages (deadlock,
# leasecontrol, orphancleanup, resultrollup, treearchive, treebudget,
# treerecovery) nest under mcpfabric/delegationtree/ rather than a separate
# top-level group, keeping the whole MCP Fabric subsystem one extractable subtree.
